The false-positive rate varies somewhat with representation width and component, particularly at small widths, but remains below 10% throughout the validation grid (Table \ref{tbl-val-fpd}). The language-model analyses use $d\geq768$, where the rates are closer to the nominal level.

```{r}
#| label: tbl-val-fpd
#| tbl-cap: "How often a component set to exactly zero is flagged, by width and by effect."
v_fp_d |>
